      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we also configure LIBSPDM_DATA_CAPABILITY_RTT_US here? Without it, libspdm uses zero transport allowance when calculating the receive timeout.\n\nOnce the helper enforces that timeout, fragmented responses can time out before reassembly completes. In our MCTP-over-USB capture, a CERTIFICATE response completed after approximately 122 ms, while the responder advertised a processing allowance of 32.768 ms.\n\nA configurable RTT would let platforms account for transport latency. Happy to provide a follow-up patch.",
