      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once receive timeouts are enforced, how should we handle delayed replies after a timeout? They could remain queued and be consumed by the next request.\n\nOne option is to close the failed socket and recreate it before the next exchange. This would require an explicit reopen path, since the socket is currently created only during initialization. It clears queued data, but does not fully prevent late replies if the kernel reuses the same tag.\n\nWould socket recreation be appropriate here, or would you recommend another recovery approach?",
